To rank points with BM25, create a full-text index on the field you want to search and set [`scoring`](/documentation/manage-data/indexing/#bm25-scoring) to `true`. For example, to search the titles of books:
{{< code-snippet path="/documentation/headless/snippets/text-search/create-title-bm25-index/" >}}
If your points already contain the field, Qdrant builds the index from the text stored in the payload, so you don't need to upload your data again.

*Available as of v1.20.0*
With scoring enabled, a full-text index can rank points by how relevant their text is to a query, using the [BM25](/documentation/search/text-search/full-text-search/#bm25) ranking function. To enable scoring, set the `scoring` type to `bm25` when you create the index:
{{< code-snippet path="/documentation/headless/snippets/create-payload-index/scoring-full-text/" >}}
